>> title: Pork Roll, Egg & Cheese
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: pork, eggs, breakfast, sandwich, griddle
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: Taylor ham egg and cheese, taylor ham egg and cheese, taylor ham, pork roll egg and cheese, pork roll, SPK, Taylor pork roll
>> servings: 2
>> time: 15 min

>> step: score four notches, griddle 3 min a side
Griddle @pork roll{6%slices}(1/4-in thick) in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) in a #skillet{} over medium-high heat ~fry{3%min} a side, after cutting four notches from the edge to the centre of each slice.

>> step: melt the cheese onto the pork
Melt @American cheese{4%slices} onto @&(~1)griddled pork roll{} in the pan, stacked three slices high so the cheese welds the pile together.

>> step: fry the eggs 2 min, yolks soft
Fry @eggs{2%large} in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) over medium heat ~fry{2%min}, basting the tops, and leave the yolks soft — the yolk is the sauce.

>> step: toast the split rolls 2 min
Toast @kaiser rolls{2}(split) cut side down on the dry griddle ~toast{2%min}.

>> step: stack pork, egg, then salt, pepper, ketchup
Stack @&(~3)cheesed pork roll{} and @&(~2)fried eggs{} on @&(~1)toasted rolls{} and finish with @kosher salt{1/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and @ketchup{2%Tbs}(30 mL).
